//! Entries slice — Batch 203 (Plan 203) — the cute-triadic-GDN pool,
//! slice A: two Linear-attention-recurrence rules (both category G).
//! Rule 1 `state-slice-resident-tiling-noninteracting-axis` (grade B):
//! when a per-head recurrent state (E*D, V) exceeds the on-chip budget,
//! tile the NON-INTERACTING value axis — one block per (row, head,
//! value-block), every interacting E-slice of the block resident for the
//! whole sequence, occupancy-halving admission. Rule 2
//! `chunk-boundary-state-checkpoint-bitwise-backward` (grade B-): the
//! forward stores the state at every chunk start in BF16 so the backward
//! is a reverse recurrence + parallel per-chunk kernels, bitwise-
//! reproducible BY CONSTRUCTION (fixed order, no fp atomics) — reproducible
//! is not exact — with the `GJ_SAVE_MASKS` store-vs-recompute rider.
//!
//! Source: `OliverSieberling/cute-triadic-gdn` @ `2caa4098073da92c2ba0d573df6453ceb7dbce45`
//! (MIT; ephemeral clone `.raw/cute-triadic-gdn` at the pin; every quote
//! re-verified VERBATIM at the pin — the real file and line recorded in-rule).
//! Paper-side figures carry the provenance label '(paper App. A via
//! riir-infer .research/007, quoted there verbatim)' — the value-axis
//! tiling law + the 512 KiB/128 KiB arithmetic are 007:37, the fixed-
//! order/no-fp-atomics determinism law 007:36, the stability law 007:30.
//!
//! Line-number drifts vs the staged plan, all corrected in-rule: the
//! header state-shape quote staged 'near lines 8-10' -> actually :7-8
//! (the sentence spans the :7->:8 line break); `_value_cols` staged
//! '~129-139' -> :129-141 (docstring :130-132, the width line :134, the
//! early return :135-136, `_TARGET_CTAS` :137-138, the occupancy return
//! :141); `cute_triadic_gdn/kernels/sm90_joint_fwd.py:91-92` verified
//! EXACT ('NV=128//VC' / 'vb,bh,b=bid%NV,(bid//NV)%H,bid//(NV*H)');
//! the sm90 backward docstring staged ':1-2' EXACT; the h table row
//! staged '~11' EXACT at :11; `_save_masks` staged '~170-175' ->
//! :167-173 (docstring :168-172, the env read :173); README.md:48-49
//! verified EXACT.
//!
//! Honesty flags: BOTH rules are mechanism rules with NO timing number.
//! Rule 1's ~70% SM fill / 32->16 halving / E>=12->16 figures are
//! in-source ADMISSION CONSTANTS (host-side `_value_cols` heuristics),
//! and the 512 KiB / 128 KiB figures are paper App. A shape arithmetic —
//! never measured wins. Rule 3's 768 MiB at 128k tokens and 'three
//! (B, T, H, 64) bf16 tensors less per layer' are in-source
